resources.string:
This app is not a safety-critical system and cannot replace the factory navigation or vehicle instruments.

· Connect, pair and change all settings while parked;
· While driving, any interaction must be done by a passenger — the driver must not hold or operate the phone;
· The wireless link can drop at any time due to interference, system sleep, hotspot switching, Bluetooth reconnection and so on, showing up as a frozen or black screen, unresponsive touch or interrupted navigation;
· A disconnect while driving can make you miss a turn, lose your route or get distracted. Always keep the factory navigation as a safety backup, and you are fully responsible for how you drive.

To work, this app requests and uses the following capabilities. Please make sure you understand them before granting:

· Shizuku (shell permission, required): to create trusted virtual displays, inject car touch input, write system compatibility settings (such as forcing apps to landscape) and read window and display state; during calls to answer / hang up, mute the microphone and route the other party's voice to the car; to feed the car microphone in as the phone microphone (voice assistant and calls); to turn on this app's own notification access and navigation accessibility service. The app does not use it to run commands unrelated to its own service;
· Notification access: to show what is playing on the car launcher; to read call notifications (caller name, photo, answer / hang-up buttons) for the car call card; to read Google Maps navigation notifications for turn hints on the cluster; optional car notification banners. Notification content is never logged or uploaded;
· Microphone: Android requires it to capture the phone's playback audio for the car; during voice or calls the car microphone replaces the phone microphone. Nothing is recorded to storage or uploaded;
· Location / nearby Wi-Fi devices: required by Android to join the car's Wi-Fi hotspot (location on Android 12, nearby devices from 13). The app does not read or store your location;
· Bluetooth: to pair with the car and set up the CarPlay link (pairing only, no Bluetooth audio connection);
· Screen recording (cast) permission: only to capture audio when "car audio" is turned on;
· Display over other apps: to start connecting in the background when the car's Bluetooth connects, and for the phone-side dim overlay;
· Accessibility service (optional, off by default): reads only the navigation text and turn / lane arrows on Amap and Waze screens, and only while the car subscribes to guidance, for cluster turn hints;
· Notifications: the ongoing connection status notification.

Pairing information, target device names, wallpapers and settings are stored only on this device and are never uploaded to any server. The app contains no analytics or advertising SDKs.
